n all pointed the same direction.", "watch": "Final vote counts from downstate and Long Island could shift the exact margin, but the outcome is settled.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Kathy Hochul (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "New York's governor race pitted incumbent-aligned Democrat Kathy Hochul against Republican Bruce Blakeman, a Trump ally from Long Island. Polling throughout the fall showed Hochul with a steady double-digit lead, including late surveys from Marist, Siena and Quinnipiac in the 12-to-18-point range. Blakeman raised over $13 million, but the money gap was modest and never translated into a polling surge.\n\nOn election night, Hochul was projected the winner by a wide margin, with AP, CBS and other outlets calling the race for her. The result matched the state's Democratic lean and the ratings consensus, which placed the contest at Likely D or better across the board.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9859, "margin": 12.77}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9584, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9776, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9779, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9761, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9756, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9778, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9799, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9796, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9804, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9807, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9805, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9817, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9754, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9752, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.99, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9892, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.